<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Stadthuys</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1660</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Stadthuys is a red-painted building in the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malacca">Malacca</a>, Malaysia, built by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> after their conquest of the city in 1641 and completed around 1660. It served as the residence of the Dutch governor and the seat of administration, and is regarded as the oldest surviving Dutch building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>. It now houses a history museum.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stadthuys.jpg" alt="Stadthuys" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User: (WT-shared) Slleong at wts wikivoyage · CC BY 1.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malacca_stadhuys1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
